  "note": "Per-cell truth for a knitting chart. consumes = live stitches taken from the row below; produces = stitches contributed to this row. Glyphs here are the on-screen chart glyphs; printed charts leave knit blank, which is an export concern rather than a table one. Charts record right-side appearance; on a wrong-side row of flat knitting the knitter works wsCounterpart. Composite increases are not chart symbols - they are two cells reassembled by the written export. Entries without wsCounterpart are unresearched, not symmetric-by-default. `pending` lists stitches the table must grow to hold and what each one needs from the schema before it can be added. `lean` says which way a stitch leans in the fabric: the drawn glyph slants that way, with a plus for increases and a minus for decreases.",
