  "pending": [
    {
      "id": "ds",
      "name": "double stitch",
      "why": "Central to shaping and German short rows. Must be drawn distinctly on the chart so the turning points are visible.",
      "notes": [
        "Count-neutral in both directions: creating a double stitch consumes 1 and produces 1, and resolving it consumes 1 and produces 1. The two integers alone therefore cannot express it.",
        "It carries state. A created double stitch must be resolved exactly once, later, in the same column. That is a column-wise invariant, unlike everything else in this table, which is row-wise. StitchDef will need a field for it - a pair id, or a marker flag.",
        "Short rows break the row invariant. A short row deliberately stops and turns, so it consumes fewer stitches than the row below produced. Row validation must know a row is short, or every short row reads as an error."
      ]
    }
  ]
